# yaml-language-server: $schema=https://rangka-os.github.io/rangka-os/schema/0.5/module.json
name: pos
version: 1.0.1
title: {id: Kasir, en: Point of sale}
summary:
  id: Kasir di browser dengan sesi kas, transaksi dan tutup sesi per outlet.
  en: A browser till with cash sessions, sales and session close per outlet.
category: sales
icon: shopping-basket-line
# The cashier of a shop or an F&B outlet, online (Jalur B v0; devices and offline come with rangka-edge, contracts
# 0003 and 0006). A cashier opens a shift (pos_shift) at an outlet with the float in the drawer, rings up sales
# (pos_sale: items or menu, qty in any unit of the item, line and receipt discounts, paid in cash with change, QRIS,
# or both), and closes the shift by counting the drawer: the difference is booked as selisih kas. Each sale is
# numbered per outlet (STRK-<outlet code>-<YYMM>-<n>, kernel contract 0009 §2a), takes its goods out of the outlet's
# stock through the declared stock rule (contract 0021; a menu item through its active recipe, contract 0022) and is
# journalled by the accounting module like a day of outlet_sales. A sale can be voided (cancel) or corrected
# (cancel, then amend without the returned items) only on its own day while its shift is open.
# Sales of an outlet run either here or through outlet_sales (Jalur A), never both: an outlet whose sales_source is
# 'kasir' takes no daily form or POS file, and a sale needs that source when outlet_sales is installed.
requires: {rangka: '>=0.5', users: ^1.2, catalogue: ^1.3, outlets: ^1.2, stock: ^1.2}
hooks: [stock.reverse_moves]
optional: {accounting: ^1.2, outlet_sales: ^1.1}
